    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d773">

                <pb facs="0826" n="814" sameAs="frus:frus1943v05/pg814"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.20210/2215: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bowers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-01-29T12:00:00-04:00">January 29,
                        1943—noon.</date><lb/>[Received 4:14 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>196. Your circular telegram January 28, 1 p.m. Repeatedly and are continuously in
                    contact with American air and steamship lines and all American concerns handling
                    strategic materials regarding sabotage, and have repeatedly discussed all this
                    in detail with Chilean Government which is completely in accord and cooperative.
                    Military Attaché<anchor n="47" xml:id="d773-f1"/> has been sent to strategic
                    points to investigate and advise and report several times and Colonel Johnson
                    has just returned from such a mission. No case of sabotage known yet though
                    suspected that the forest fires in the south may be ascribable to Axis
                    agents.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d773-f1" n="47" xml:id="d773-f1-content">
                <p>Col. Wendell Gunner Johnson.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
